{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-steampipe-api-v1",
    "name": "Steampipe Cloud Governance API",
    "description": "Stage 1 API for multi-tenant Steampipe executions.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this collection **and** an environment from `postman/environments/`.\n2. Select the environment (top-right): **Steampipe \u2014 Local** or **Steampipe \u2014 Remote (Docker)**.\n3. Run **Smoke Test Workflow** or individual folders \u2014 test scripts save IDs to the **environment**.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Seeded DB (`python scripts/seed_dummy_data.py`)\n- Running worker for execution endpoints\n\nOpenAPI: {{baseUrl}}/docs\n\nSee `postman/README.md` for Newman and variable conventions.\n\n## Headers (every request)\n| Header | Value | When |\n|--------|-------|------|\n| `Accept` | `application/json` | Always |\n| `Content-Type` | `application/json` | POST / PUT / PATCH with body |\n| `Authorization` | `Bearer {{authToken}}` | When `authToken` is set in environment |\n\nAuth is configured at **collection level** (Authorization \u2192 Bearer Token). See folder **Authentication** for details.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{authToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Require an active Postman environment",
          "const baseUrl = pm.environment.get('baseUrl');",
          "if (!baseUrl) {",
          "    throw new Error('Select a Steampipe environment (Local or Remote Docker) before sending requests.');",
          "}",
          "",
          "// Standard headers (visible in request Headers tab after send, or add explicitly below)",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Accept', value: 'application/json' });",
          "",
          "// JSON body requests",
          "if (['POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH'].includes(pm.request.method)) {",
          "    const body = pm.request.body;",
          "    if (body && body.mode === 'raw' && body.raw) {",
          "        pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Content-Type', value: 'application/json' });",
          "    }",
          "}",
          "",
          "// Auth: collection uses Bearer {{authToken}} (Authorization tab \u2192 Inherit from parent)",
          "const token = pm.environment.get('authToken');",
          "if (!token && pm.request.auth && pm.request.auth.type === 'bearer') {",
          "    // Dev mode: API_AUTH_REQUIRED=false \u2014 no token needed",
          "    pm.request.auth = { type: 'noauth' };",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test('Response time under 10s', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(10000);",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "description": "How auth works with this API.\n\n- **Dev (default):** `API_AUTH_REQUIRED=false` \u2014 leave `authToken` empty; Authorization header is skipped automatically.\n- **Production:** set `authToken` in the active environment; collection sends `Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}`.\n\nNote: JWT validation is not wired in Stage 1 yet (`src/api/deps.py`). Headers are included for forward compatibility.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "How auth works (read me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/docs",
            "description": "OpenAPI docs. No auth required in dev.\n\n**Environment variable:** `authToken`\n\n**Header sent:** `Authorization: Bearer <token>`"
          },
          "auth": {
            "type": "inherit"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
